From 5992c5c5547d3154f3bfd8c749b8e5e7edaaab98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop extract_skyline reading hazy distant ridges as sky

A distant ridge under haze against an overcast sky is pale and grey enough
to pass the absolute luminance and saturation test, so the trace dropped to
the dark near treeline below it and the horizon read low. Optimistic,
plausible and silent. FINDINGS-anchor.md section 6.

A pixel now also has to stay within sky_tol (default 60) of the running
mean of the sky just above it. The reference follows the sky down the
column so gradients and cloud texture pass. The default comes from the
2026-07-30 Candamo frame: hazy ridges step ~90 levels from the sky there,
cloud texture ~27 at the 99.999th percentile and 50 at worst. On that
frame the trace now sits on the distant ridge crests, 1.2 to 2.8 deg above
the old trace depending on sector.

Tests: a hazy ridge with colours sampled from that frame (fails on the old
code), and a cloudy sky with gradient and patches (fails if the tolerance
is set tight enough to trip on clouds). Exposed as --sky-tol and named in
the trace check warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
